      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2010 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The SAR study of a series of 6-aryloxymethyl-8-aryl substituted quinolines is described. Optimization of the series led to the discovery of compound 26b, a highly potent (IC50=0.6 nM) and selective PDE4D inhibitor with a 75-fold selectivity over the A, B, and C subtypes and over 18,000-fold selectivity against other PDE family members. Rat pharmacokinetics and tissue distribution are also summarized."
      },
